# The scenes of the recorded-http-responses deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# recorded-http-responses.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in recorded-http-responses.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: step 1, the version catalogue
note "Step 1: add WireMock to the version catalogue."
show libs.versions.toml "/wiremock/" gradle/libs.versions.toml

## Scene 2: step 2, the test dependency
note "Step 2: add it as a test dependency of the lesson."
show lessons/recorded-http-responses/example/build.gradle.kts "/^dependencies/" "lesson build file" --zoom 11

## Scene 3: the code under test
note "The code under test: today's postcode client. It reads a town from *every* answer."
show TodaysPostcodeClient 16 19 "today's postcode client" --zoom 18

## Scene 4: the test against the real service
note "A test against the supplier's *real* service: it needs the network and an account."
show RealSupplierTest 14 18 "the test against the real service" --zoom 15

## Scene 5: a recorded answer
note "A *recorded* answer: the request, and what the supplier sent back. Here, an outage."
show lessons/recorded-http-responses/example/src/test/resources/supplier/mappings/supplier-outage.json 1 8 "recorded answer" --zoom 4-6

## Scene 6: making recordings from a stand-in
note "Making recordings: WireMock passes each question to a *stand-in* supplier on this machine, and keeps the answer."
show RecordingTest 48 59 "a stand-in supplier, and the recorder" --mark 50-51
show RecordingTest 83 98 "making recordings" --zoom 85-86

## Scene 7: the tests for recordings
note "Recordings copy real answers, so they can hold *personal data*. Today they are saved as recorded."
show RecordingTest 67 81 "tests for the saved recordings" --zoom 78

## Scene 8: the tests with recordings
note "Tests with WireMock: it replays every recording on a local port."
show RecordedSupplierTest 18 45 "tests with recorded answers" --zoom 18-19

## Scene 9: the recordings find two bugs, and personal data
note "Run the tests against today's code:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:recorded-http-responses:test -Pcode=today"
callout "The recordings show two bugs in the client, and the saved files hold a name, an email address and a token."

## Scene 10: the cleaner
note "The masking step: drop the token, and swap each name and email address for a *keyed* substitute."
show KeyedRecordingCleaner 43 63 "the masking step" --zoom 57
show KeyedRecordingCleaner 100 110 "the keyed substitute" --mark 103-105

## Scene 11: the fix
note "The client that checks what the supplier said first, and the masking step:"
show PostcodeClient 18 26 "the fixed client" --zoom 21-24
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:recorded-http-responses:test"
callout "Every recorded answer is handled, and no personal data is saved, with no network and no account."
